{
 "title": "E4 Similarity is not novelty",
 "question": "Do the indicators agree with each other, and are the generated ideas new or recombinations of this literature?",
 "findings": [
  "Semantic similarity and the share of known concept pairs correlate at ρ = 0.41 over all items, so they do not measure the same thing.",
  "Of 96 generated ideas in 6 topics: 32 near-duplicates of a prior paper, 27 known combinations, 37 new combinations of this literature.",
  "1 idea is less similar to any paper than the median idea, yet every one of its concept pairs already appears together in some prior paper: low similarity without new combinations."
